					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SINEOSCILLATOR\n\nThe Sine oscillator generates values by using a sinoid waveform. \nA Sine oscillates from its minimal value to its maximum value. \n\nThe speed of the oscillation is controlled by the frequency.\nThe range of values is set by the amplitude.\nThe offset is added to the output.\n\nPhase offset controls where in the phase of the waveform the value starts.\nThis is mostly used when instancing the oscillator to get different values from each instance.\n\nIn the node panel \/ hidden in the node, you’ll find the Reset Phase and Unipolar parameters.\n\nReset Phase will reset the oscillator to its phase offset point.\n\nUnipolar will limit the output of the oscillator to be either negative or positive. \nThis depends on whether the amplitude is negative or not."
					}
				},
